    "Shared namespaces produce disjoint subtree-to-host routes for split and combined deployments; subtree maps are immutable and same-owner nested roots collapse.",
    "Whole-namespace and nested different-owner conflicts fail during planning across different hosts; malformed or unconstructable metadata readers cannot silently reserve routes.",
    "Actual MVC module selection mounts the shared prefix once, preserves legacy aliases, nested paths and inherited interface mappings, and leaves unselected controllers absent.",
    "Wrong-owner paths, unowned wildcard captures and segment-prefix confusion reject without depending on HTTP method or registration order.",
    "Composed conditional-controller mappings are read without initializing their deliberately failing static initializer; planning ignores deployment conditions when reserving ownership.",
    "Duplicate controller resources and configuration/controller ClassLoader mismatch reject before runtime.",
    "Environment placeholders, relative paths, dot traversal before and after variables, and duplicate slashes reject; stable roots before variables are derived.",
    "Actual Common identity, OIDC and i18n controller classes produce compatible split/combined routes with unchanged URLs; tests use explicit metadata-only module fixtures, not production module assembly.",
    "Existing exclusive namespaces, extra MVC handler mappings, legacy gateway-stripped hosting, selected-module isolation and workflow HTTP regression remain passing.",
    "Pure composition runtime dependency gate confirms no Spring/web dependency; module JARs contain the exact newly compiled planning and servlet classes."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No production Common/OIDC/i18n HTTP adapter extraction or component-scan ownership migration is claimed. Common tests use metadata-only fixture module declarations; a full modular business host is not started.",
    "Common was filtered to the new planning test. Other four listed test projects ran their full test tasks; no full repository or production business suite was run.",
    "Paths are reserved as literal subtrees, not partitioned by request method/headers/query conditions. Shared mode requires a type-level mapping with a stable first segment; whole-namespace mode remains available.",
    "Metadata readers are trusted application adapters with a public no-argument constructor. The supplied servlet reader is bounded and metadata-only; this interface is not an untrusted-code sandbox.",
    "Runtime dynamic-plugin mapping additions and full browser/security/data/permissions flows remain part of later integration acceptance; initialization validation is not a replacement.",
    "No frontend changes, frontend tests, service distribution rebuild, deployment, production configuration/database writes, commit or push in this increment.",
    "Gateway/config publication, complete resource-owner adoption, remaining HTTP/frontend/security composition, formal standalone service and three-topology acceptance remain outstanding."
  ],
